From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: let a tx frame skip the TCP ACK filter if
 allocation fails

rwnx_start_xmit() allocates a struct msg_buf for every frame of at most
MAX_TCP_ACK (200) bytes before asking the TCP ACK filter.
intf_tcp_alloc_msg() uses kzalloc(GFP_ATOMIC), prints on failure and
then memset()s the result anyway, and the caller writes msgbuf->rwnx_vif
right after. A failed allocation is a NULL dereference in the transmit
path for every small frame.

intf_tcp_alloc_msg() no longer touches a NULL result (the memset() is
dropped, kzalloc() already zeroes), and rwnx_start_xmit() skips the
filter when it gets NULL. The frame is sent unfiltered.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c
index 1e5c254..feec72e 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_tcp_ack.c
@@ -10,7 +10,6 @@ struct msg_buf *intf_tcp_alloc_msg(struct msg_buf *msg)
 	msg = kzalloc(len , GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if(!msg)
 		printk("%s: alloc failed \n", __func__);
-	memset(msg,0,len);
 	return msg;
 }
 						
diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
index 27adde5..ab01720 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
@@ -1467,8 +1467,8 @@ netdev_tx_t rwnx_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *dev)
 		skb->priority = 0;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_FILTER_TCP_ACK
-	if(cpu_to_le16(skb->len) <= MAX_TCP_ACK){
-        msgbuf=intf_tcp_alloc_msg(msgbuf);
+	if(cpu_to_le16(skb->len) <= MAX_TCP_ACK &&
+	   (msgbuf = intf_tcp_alloc_msg(msgbuf)) != NULL){
         msgbuf->rwnx_vif=rwnx_vif;
         msgbuf->skb=skb;
         if(filter_send_tcp_ack(rwnx_hw,msgbuf,skb->data,cpu_to_le16(skb->len))){
